Cosmos look: dark title bars, the Cosmos icon when a program has none, Cosmos in the bottle-update window.

- winemac: Mac Driver option Appearance. By default every Wine window, title
  bar and Mac dialog uses macOS's dark appearance (NSAppearanceNameDarkAqua),
  like Cosmopolitan. "light" forces light, "system" follows macOS. Read with
  the other options before the Cocoa app starts.
- winemac: a program without an icon of its own showed macOS's generic app
  icon (CrossOver's hack 13440 only finds CrossOver.app's exeIcon.icns through
  CX_ROOT). Without CX_ROOT it now takes share/wine/cosmos/exeIcon.icns from
  the engine, found next to winemac.so.
- wineboot: the window shown while a bottle is created or updated says
  "Cosmos is getting the bottle in ... ready" under the title "Cosmos". Its
  icon is user32's IDI_WINLOGO, which the Cosmos build replaces with the
  Cosmos icon (cosmos-theme/oic_winlogo.ico).

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m
index 869b3c7..134423b 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_main.m
@@ -74,6 +74,12 @@ static void run_cocoa_app(void* info)
             created_app = TRUE;
         }
 
+        /* Cosmos: dark title bars and Mac dialogs (Mac Driver "Appearance"; see setup_options) */
+        if (app_appearance == 0)
+            [NSApp setAppearance:[NSAppearance appearanceNamed:NSAppearanceNameDarkAqua]];
+        else if (app_appearance == 1)
+            [NSApp setAppearance:[NSAppearance appearanceNamed:NSAppearanceNameAqua]];
+
         /* CrossOver hack 12205: Prevent call to NSVersionOfRunTimeLibrary() during app startup.
                                  It can crash if a Wine thread unloads a dylib simultaneously. */
         [[NSUserDefaults standardUserDefaults] registerDefaults:
